    hook: "Dr. Bessel van der Kolk spent 40 years treating trauma and wrote one of the most important mental health books of the 21st century: 'The Body Keeps the Score.' His central finding: trauma is not just a psychological experience stored in memories — it is a physiological event that reorganizes how the body manages perceptions of threat. Trauma survivors often experience their past as physically present — their nervous systems remain on high alert, their bodies respond to reminders with intense physiological reactions, and they may struggle to feel safe even when they are objectively safe. Understanding trauma — how it works and how it heals — is essential for both personal wellbeing and for understanding the people around you.",
