    hook: "Dr. Mark Hyman, a Harvard-trained physician and 12-time New York Times bestselling author, describes conventional medicine as 'sick care' rather than healthcare — a system organized to treat disease after it manifests rather than to prevent it or address its root causes. He practices functional medicine: an approach that asks 'why is this person sick?' rather than 'what drug treats this symptom?' Both systems have genuine strengths and genuine limitations. Understanding both — and how to navigate between them — is one of the most practical health skills you can develop.",
